==Battleground==
*5 [[One Horn]]s spawn, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Assassin Bear]]s spawn as bosses after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
'''Don't kill the One Horns!''' Because the enemy limit is 3, defeating any of the One Horns will make room for the Assassin Bears to spawn. To avoid that, use anti-Red units capable of causing knockback (as One Horn has only one knockback, raw damage should not be used to keep them at bay) like [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Dread Pirate Catley]],[[Boogie Cat (Special Cat)|Gato Amigo]], [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and [[Bean Cats (Special Cat)|Brah/Val Val Cats]]. Use [[Cat Combo]]s if you feel you do not have enough starting cash, as defeating the One Horns for funding is out of the question. Since they aren't bosses, they can be pushed behind the base while said CC units slowly demolish it.

This strategy becomes easier as the Crown difficulty increases since each One Horn has more health, thereby reducing the chances of failure.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Axis of Evil]] stages, Merciless Onslaught has a Russian-themed Japanese name. In this case, Poppō Ryōdo (ポッポー領土, "Poppō Territory") is a pun on ''Hoppō Ryōdo'' (北方領土), meaning "Northern Territories" - as in the [[wikipedia:Kuril Islands dispute|Northern Territories dispute]] between Japan and the Russian Federation.

